    "turn_text": "The best definition of the federal government came from Ezra Klein who once said that the federal government is an insurance firm with an army. And so Medicaid is one of the core functions of the federal government, even though it's seen as less politically sacrosanct as Medicare. Medicaid is no less important. Medicaid is the largest payer of health care and long-term care in the nation. It is the health insurance program for the lowest income. And it's the long-term care program for the elderly and the chronically ill and the disabled. And even though we think of Medicare as a program for the elderly, Medicaid is just as important. to the elderly. The elderly and the disabled benefit disproportionately from Medicaid. In New York, the elderly and the disabled make up 20% of Medicaid enrollments, but account for 60% of Medicaid expenditure. So it is as critical a program for the elderly as Medicare.",
