    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "It just makes me tired, man. I don't know. I feel so grim talking about this. And I don't know. I'm in the middle of it in the sense that I talk about politics all the time. And my day job is hosting this podcast and writing about this stuff. But you're really in the middle of it. And do you ever just get tired of this nonsense? I'm trying not to swear too much. It just seems like every couple of years, you know, we have a different culture war fight and Republicans, you know, they leverage some culture war nonsense to get into power. But once they're here, it's always the same thing. It's always, we want to cut social security, Medicare and Medicaid, and we want to provide tax cuts for the rich. Because that's the context for this is that they want to provide about five trillion dollars worth of tax cuts that would go almost all to very wealthy people, and you know, gutting Medicaid is one of the ways they want to pay for it. And it's just, this is an almost an unprofessional line of questioning, but do you ever just get tired of it? It's just crazy.",
