  {
    "episode_id": 71080,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71080.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "It feels to me, government at every level is broken. Our politics is broken. And you know, certainly the frontal assaults on Medicaid is causing me sleepless nights because my district would be hit the hardest. And you know, it feels like we live in a morally inverted universe in the age of Donald Trump. You know, the Donald Trump and congressional Republicans are proposing to cut Nutritional assistance, by up to $230 billion, education, by up to $330 billion, healthcare, by up to $880 billion, in order to fund trillions of dollars in tax cuts, whose benefits will largely flow toward the top 1%. It is as egregious a misplacement of our national priorities, as I could imagine. And we're witnessing an unprecedented decimation of the federal workforce. And I worry that we could see an unprecedented evisceration of the social safety net upon which tens of millions of Americans depend. There are about 100 million Americans who depend on Medicaid, who benefit from Medicaid, directly or indirectly.",
