    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, Medicaid matters to the public and the burden falls on us to give it the attention that it deserves. I was on Morning Joe and I was asked about Donald Trump's executive order, attacking DEI. And I said, obviously I disagree with his executive orders, but I'll be honest with you, I represent a district that is overwhelmingly Latino and African and American. I never had a constituent approach me and tell me, Congressman, my highest priority is diversity, equity, and inclusion. Like my constituents typically tell me my highest priority is housing, healthcare, public safety, the cost of living. And so I've long been of the view that we should ignore the fashionable nonsense, the culture wars, the three letter acronyms, CRT and DEI and ESG, and focus on the issues that matter to people, the bread and butter issues of healthcare and housing and the cost of living and public safety. I've been advocating for a return to the basics because that's what resonates",
