    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "voters and with people. Now, one of the conversations that's happening at the same time we talk about the budget resolution, we mentioned Doge and there are people who are concerned about the idea of waste, fraud, and abuse. And that seems to be the three word magic phrase that they're using to justify cuts in hundreds of different programs, whatever they want to cut is simply waste, fraud, and abuse. And I don't think that Doge is doing that in any sort of good faith. But if there are people out there who say, well, you know, we should care about that stuff. Can't we make Medicaid a little bit better? Can't we, you know, isn't there some areas of fraud or waste that we could attack? How would you respond to that to people who are not working for Doge but who've heard that and are like, well, yeah, we should deal with that. Are there areas of waste that we can cut? Are there smart things we can do? Or is this whole effort just entirely misguided needs to be shut down at the core?",
