    "turn_text": "It's unclear to me because there are a number of countries that have single payer systems like Canada or single payer and single provider systems, like the British health system, but those systems have challenges as well. It's a trade-off, right? So you might get more health coverage, but you might get less than the way of quality. So the American system feels so radically different. from any other health system in the world, and certainly an industrialized world. I feel like we have to, how do we restructure the incentives of the healthcare system to reward actual outcomes?",
