  {
    "episode_id": 71080,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71080.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "Returning to the point about waste, fraud, and abuse, the entire healthcare industry and system and the massively complex tangle of stuff that we've got going on, there's a lot of inefficiency, I would say, in our entire system, and it's not just government inefficiency, The private healthcare is notoriously inefficient in a lot of ways, too. Certainly, there's ways we can make this better. One of the numbers that I've seen is about 5% of Medicaid payment money is called improper payments. That can mean different things. It can be overpayments or it can be lack of documentation. But I think we can work on that 5% while not taking a hatchet to the program that would really gut coverage for the poorest people in society. I think we can walk and chew gum at the same time here.",
